{"parentUuid":"8781fd18-842e-45bf-8994-c8ea70a4b6b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_011UtX5x9btJyneBCz9NTtvW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is that the UI (JavaScript in the browser) is calling `/cors-test/api/run.php` directly via fetch, and it's getting HTML back. This means run.php is returning HTML instead of JSON.\n\nWait, actually - looking at the error message again: `SyntaxError: Unexpected token '<', \"<!DOCTYPE \"... is not valid JSON`. The browser's JavaScript is getting HTML from somewhere.\n\nThe UI calls run.php which is a server-side proxy. But if the browser is getting HTML, it means run.php itself is returning HTML (a PHP error page) or there's some server redirect happening.\n \nSo the HTML response is likely coming from a PHP error being output before the JSON, or possibly a WAF/firewall on the gabia hosting intercepting the POST requests and returning an error page. Another possibility is that `display_errors` is enabled and outputting error messages as HTML instead of letting the JSON response through.\n\nActually, wait - I see that `display_errors` is explicitly set to 0 in bootstrap.php, but that happens after config loading. If there's a fatal error during the config phase, it could output HTML before that setting takes effect. The config file looks syntactically correct though, so that's probably not it.\n\nI should look at the ui/index.php to see how the requests are actually being made - maybe the UI is making direct cross-origin requests from the browser rather than proxying through the server, which would explain why it's getting HTML responses instead of JSON.\n\nThe error message is clear: JavaScript is trying to parse HTML as JSON. The fetch is getting an HTML response body instead of JSON. Most likely, either run.php itself is broken and returns HTML for any request, or something in the request chain - maybe a WAF or parent .htaccess on bluesquare's hosting - is intercepting the POST to run.php and returning an error page. Could also be a PHP 7.4 compatibility issue in run.php that's causing it to fail before outputting JSON.\n\nThe best diagnostic would be to directly test what run.php returns, but I can't do that. Let me look at how ui/index.php is making these fetch calls to understand the request structure better.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7087,"cache_read_input_tokens":48467,"output_tokens":882,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7087,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":882,"cache_read_input_tokens":48467,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7087},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaVdCqi4GMeX6GYdkPget","type":"assistant","uuid":"97743c9c-cd3c-4b4c-817f-62ff85ceae59","timestamp":"2026-04-28T05:34:48.655Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\최신프로젝트\\인터파크\\백업\\260427","sessionId":"59c7642a-71bc-4ae8-a885-c0624014856b","version":"2.1.121","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
