{"parentUuid":"4d06fea4-44b5-47b3-b81a-e919b0265e90","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_017MGZESUM6Yi7CjV8jwHmUi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The noltheater server is still getting 400 from bluesquare on all requests. The fact that it's still happening after our header rename means either:\n1. The new run.php wasn't uploaded to noltheater (or bluesquare's guard.php wasn't updated)\n2. The WAF is still blocking based on something else\n\nBut wait - we can't see the actual request headers in this error output. Let me check if the request shows the old or new headers. Actually the user didn't share the full request details this time.\n\nThe key question is: is bluesquare's WAF still blocking? And what headers is noltheater sending now?\n\n\nActually, I'm realizing the URL path itself might be the culprit - `/cors-test/api/cors-probe.php` contains \"cors\" and \"probe\" which could trigger the WAF independently of the headers we renamed.\n\nBut that doesn't make sense either, since bluesquare's A tests use the same URL paths and work fine when calling noltheater. The real puzzle is why this is one-directional - noltheater calling bluesquare gets blocked with a 400, but the reverse works. Both servers are on the same host, so I'd expect consistent WAF behavior unless bluesquare's WAF is specifically configured to be stricter on inbound requests, or maybe the 400 isn't actually from the WAF at all but from bluesquare's PHP not handling the request properly.\n\nLet me think about what A1-A7 are actually doing - noltheater's run.php is making curl GET requests to bluesquare's api/whoami.php with custom headers like X-Sync-Ts, X-Sync-Sig, and X-Sync-Host. The 400 response is suspicious because our PHP code only returns 400 for specific cases, and authentication failures return 401. So either bluesquare's Apache is rejecting the request before PHP even runs, or those custom headers are triggering the WAF.\n\nLooking at the actual headers from the A7 result, I'm seeing the old header names like X-Cors-Test-Ts and X-Cors-Test-Host - which means the updated run.php with the new header names hasn't been deployed to noltheater yet. That's why the requests are still failing.\n\nI should ask the user directly if they've completed uploading the deploy-noltheater folder to FTP, or just request the current request headers from A7 to confirm whether the header names have changed.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":551,"cache_read_input_tokens":93226,"output_tokens":1234,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":551,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":1234,"cache_read_input_tokens":93226,"cache_creation_input_tokens":551,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":551},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaVeSzSBQNnKzxF9NF96k","type":"assistant","uuid":"939e83d7-fc1a-4891-a076-d3debc1e0b48","timestamp":"2026-04-28T05:51:12.649Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\최신프로젝트\\인터파크\\백업\\260427","sessionId":"59c7642a-71bc-4ae8-a885-c0624014856b","version":"2.1.121","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
