{"parentUuid":"134f4b9c-96e3-492c-bced-414f56141549","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_012kNKx23nibx7s5nmfhUAej","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The request to run.php on noltheater returned 200 OK - that's the browser→noltheater request. That's working fine.\n\nBut the issue is what noltheater sends to bluesquare (server-to-server). I need to see the response body of run.php, specifically the `request.headers` field that shows what headers noltheater used when calling bluesquare.\n\nThe user showed me the browser's request/response headers for the run.php call itself, not the internal headers that run.php uses when calling bluesquare.\n\nI need to see the A7 result's `data.request.headers` - which shows what curl headers noltheater sent to bluesquare.\n\n\nSo I should tell them to check the Response tab in their browser's developer tools and look for the `data.request.headers` array within the response body - that's where the actual headers noltheater sent to bluesquare will be visible.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":726,"cache_read_input_tokens":95043,"output_tokens":393,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":726,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":393,"cache_read_input_tokens":95043,"cache_creation_input_tokens":726,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":726},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaVeYQjJuSZjX7A4NzPSg","type":"assistant","uuid":"a498c550-ce5e-41db-89e4-2082bfc24f30","timestamp":"2026-04-28T05:52:10.130Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\최신프로젝트\\인터파크\\백업\\260427","sessionId":"59c7642a-71bc-4ae8-a8