{"parentUuid":"7d6c750c-274d-4124-83e6-2ef1d4bc1747","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01TpCat5KNujzgF398AzDDEW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see two problems:\n\n1. **Bluesquare's run.php is also still using old headers** (`X-Cors-Test-Ts`, `User-Agent: cors-test/1.0`) when calling noltheater. This means bluesquare's run.php also wasn't updated properly.\n\n2. **Noltheater's ping.php is reading `X-Sync-Ts`/`X-Sync-Sig`** (because we updated guard.php) but bluesquare is sending `X-Cors-Test-Ts` - so noltheater's guard says `missing_auth` because it can't find the headers.\n   \nSo the issue is symmetric: both services updated their guards to expect the new headers, but neither updated their outgoing requests, so they're each sending old headers to the other and getting rejected.\n\nThe fix is straightforward—I need to upload the updated run.php files from the local deploy folders to both servers' FTP directories to sync the header names across the board.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1291,"cache_read_input_tokens":97976,"output_tokens":873,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1291,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":3,"output_tokens":873,"cache_read_input_tokens":97976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1291,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1291},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CaVenXWEqnvo2P6dw5mxK","type":"assistant","uuid":"caaa3821-50a2-48ec-8638-ff81b624fb96","timestamp":"2026-04-28T05:55:24.837Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"d:\\최신프로젝트\\인터파크\\백업\\260427","sessionId":"59c7642a-71bc-4ae8-a885-c0624014856b","ver