{"parentUuid":"57b23e15-903a-4bf0-a217-e90f0f083311","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_01BKEpfnjJuJEDWWnXqz1v12","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the selected file - deploy-bluesquare/api/run.php - it already has the correct headers (`X-Sync-Ts`, `X-Sync-Host`, `User-Agent: PHP/7.4`). So the local file is correct.\n\nBut the server is still returning `X-Cors-Test-Ts` in the A2 ping_peer test. This means:\n1. The file was uploaded but the server is caching the old PHP file (PHP opcode cache/OPcache)\n2. The wrong file was uploaded\n\nWait - actually looking at the A2 result, the URL is `https://www.noltheater-daehakro.com/cors-test/api/ping.php` - this is bluesquare calling noltheater, not noltheater calling bluesquare. \n\nAnd bluesquare's run.php is sending `X-Cors-Test-Ts`. But the local deploy-bluesquare/api/run.php shows `X-Sync-Ts`, so either the FTP upload didn't actually overwrite the server file or PHP OPcache on the Gabia shared hosting is serving the old compiled version instead of the newly uploaded one.\n\nThe most straightforward approach would be to have the user wait a few minutes for OPcache to expire, then test again—or verify the upload actually succeeded by checking the file timestamp directly on the FTP server.\n\nLooking at the response headers more carefully, the A2 result shows `X-Cors-Test-Ts` while the local version has `X-Sync-Ts`, which suggests either the upload didn't overwrite the file or OPcache is still serving the old version. I should ask them to check the actual file on FTP to confirm it contains the updated header, or verify whether Gabia has OPcache reset functionality available.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5747,"cache_read_input_tokens":100642,"output_tokens":1017,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0}